  "adaptations": [
    "schema.sql contains only the sessions fixture prerequisite; no unrelated application tables.",
    "Owner-reviewed automatic speech files and additional auth-gate test dependencies copied from PR240 commit 1829fb311d74aae09d50b9ad202a9dce106e5d63. _redirects contains the relevant Admin and Sir David SQL rules only; other website routes are excluded.",
    "Claude host API tests are now copied intact with existing portal/session fixture dependencies. Canonical adapter lives in ../local-adapter; the export retains its own build script for that layout. The local bridge and source tests are exported separately; its setup ZIP is copied exactly from the reviewed host commit.",
    "Export build regenerates the adapter bundle from ../local-adapter; the source-location comment differs from the host bundle, while canonical source and runtime code are preserved.",
    "Workspace tools and current Admin/adapter source synchronized from reviewed host commit 85e466e309ba3dcbbb09342afe21b73b25cdf663. Root-scoped history and rollback on backup/journal failure are included. Local configuration, history and user files remain excluded. The export build retains its own module-source path.",
    "Claude fetch receiver hotfix and cache index synchronized with reviewed host 27a1a5dc3312d2055a14a07e6591c5465b38f668. Export bundle preserves its own module-source location comment.",
    "Planner candidate adds owner-scoped projects, events, reminder claims and delegated Outlook integration on the existing companion export. Migration 010 is reserved with the host owner. Native 1.3 is a separate build; host deployment and Microsoft user consent are separate acceptance steps.",
    "Work windows synchronized from host PR307 3be3457816ffa26a85d86f39d00c7031a52183c2 (unchanged on host main ae33bfecc6323d52480e8871b7d70617d373ac7e): planner client, CSS, route, API, work-window module, migration 012, private calendar schema and the work-window UI test are byte-identical to host. Export adaptations: src/site/sir-david-calendar-dispatch.js answers GET /api/calendar/events from private_calendar_events only (the host router also merges Proton ICS and routine-imported Outlook rows), and the work-window API test builds into a temporary folder instead of the host planning folder."
  ],
